ops/codex/build-sandbox-limits.log:296:6. Root-cause before any gold/null rerun. From the runs/gold-null2 logs, find task 39/52 and the two exit-124 tasks. Prime suspect: `timeout` kills only the direct child, so orphaned pytest or grandchild processes kept growing. Fix it in the sandbox runner. Each task gets its own process group or systemd-run scope with MemoryMax=4G and 2 CPUs, which also matches the scorer sandbox (4 GiB, 2 vCPU). On timeout, kill the whole group, and assert no survivors before the next task. Log peak RSS per task. Send it to codex-review and add a unit test that spawns an orphaning child.
ops/codex/build-sandbox-limits.log:310:- Since the 17:30 reboot there's no systemd user manager: /run/user/1001/bus is missing, linger is off, and our processes run in system.slice/cron.service. So bin/job takes its FALLBACK path, `ulimit -v 5G` per process. That limit doesn't cap a job's process tree: N parallel pytest workers can each reach 5G. A parallel gold run could OOM the 12 GB box again (no swap) as things stand.
